<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="Ptx1" class="ltx_part">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_part">Appendices</h2>

<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs of Theoretical Analysis</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of Results in Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Estimability ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide the proofs of Lemmas <a href="#S3.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ Impossibility for the green-red list watermark. ‣ 3.2 Estimability ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, <a href="#S3.Thmlem2" title="Lemma 3.2. ‣ Identifiability for continuous pivotal statistics. ‣ 3.2 Estimability ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, and <a href="#S3.Thmlem3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ Identifiability for continuous pivotal statistics. ‣ 3.2 Estimability ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> in this subsection.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlem1" title="Lemma 3.1. ‣ Impossibility for the green-red list watermark. ‣ 3.2 Estimability ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Each data point is equivalently i.i.d. from <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Ber}((1-{\varepsilon})\gamma+{\varepsilon}\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Ber</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Ber}((1-{\varepsilon})\gamma+{\varepsilon}\mu)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since both <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> are unknown, there are multiple combinations of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\varepsilon},\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\varepsilon},\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> that yield the same value for <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-{\varepsilon})\gamma+{\varepsilon}\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-{\varepsilon})\gamma+{\varepsilon}\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, resulting in the same data distribution.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlem2" title="Lemma 3.2. ‣ Identifiability for continuous pivotal statistics. ‣ 3.2 Estimability ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ Identifiability for continuous pivotal statistics. ‣ 3.2 Estimability ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, we have three key conditions: (i) <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is known, (ii) <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim\limits_{x\to 0}\frac{\bar{F}(x)}{F_{0}(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim\limits_{x\to 0}\frac{\bar{F}(x)}{F_{0}(x)}</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by the population distribution of observed <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>, and (iii) <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim\limits_{x\to 0}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)}{F_{0}(x)}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim\limits_{x\to 0}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)}{F_{0}(x)}=0</annotation></semantics></math> since all NTP distributions are non-singular.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">From (<a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 3.3 Estimation Methods ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), for any <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{F}(x)=(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}(x)+{\varepsilon}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{F}(x)=(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}(x)+{\varepsilon}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 3.3 Estimation Methods ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Dividing both sides by <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and taking the limit as <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 0}\frac{\bar{F}(x)}{F_{0}(x)}=(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\cdot\lim_{x\to 0}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)}{F_{0}(x)}=(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\cdot 0=1-{\varepsilon}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.055em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 0}\frac{\bar{F}(x)}{F_{0}(x)}=(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\cdot\lim_{x\to 0}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)}{F_{0}(x)}=(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\cdot 0=1-{\varepsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}=1-\lim_{x\to 0}\frac{\bar{F}(x)}{F_{0}(x)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}=1-\lim_{x\to 0}\frac{\bar{F}(x)}{F_{0}(x)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since the right-hand side consists only of known or determined quantities, we conclude that <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is identifiable.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlem3" title="Lemma 3.3. ‣ Identifiability for continuous pivotal statistics. ‣ 3.2 Estimability ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">It suffices to prove that the null and alternative CDFs (as shown in Table <a href="#S2.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ A general framework for watermarking. ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) of the considered watermarks satisfy Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ Identifiability for continuous pivotal statistics. ‣ 3.2 Estimability ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>. We examine each watermark separately.

<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gumbel-max watermark:</span>
The CDFs are given by</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{0}(x)=x,~~\text{and}~~F_{\bm{P}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{0}(x)=x,~~\text{and}~~F_{\bm{P}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{{w}}P_{{w}}x^{1/P_{{w}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>w</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{{w}}P_{{w}}x^{1/P_{{w}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}=(P_{1},\ldots,P_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}=(P_{1},\ldots,P_{|{{\mathcal{W}}}|})</annotation></semantics></math> is non-singular, we have <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/P_{{w}}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/P_{{w}}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{w}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{w}\in{{\mathcal{W}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}^{\prime}(0)=1&gt;F_{\bm{P}}^{\prime}(0)=0~~\implies~~\lim_{x\to 0}\frac{F_{\bm{P}}(x)}{F_{0}(x)}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.938em" rspace="0.660em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}^{\prime}(0)=1&gt;F_{\bm{P}}^{\prime}(0)=0~~\implies~~\lim_{x\to 0}\frac{F_{\bm{P}}(x)}{F_{0}(x)}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inverse transform watermark:<span id="A1.SS1.p5.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. [20]</a></cite>, we consider the condition <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{(2)}\cdot\log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{(2)}\cdot\log|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{{\mathcal{W}}}|\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th largest probability in <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑷</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. The CDFs are:</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F_{0}(x)=x^{2},~~\text{and}~~F_{\bm{P}}(x)=\left[1-\frac{1-x}{P_{(1)}}\right]_{[0,1]}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F_{0}(x)=x^{2},~~\text{and}~~F_{\bm{P}}(x)=\left[1-\frac{1-x}{P_{(1)}}\right]_{[0,1]}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[x]_{[0,1]}:=\max\{\min\{x,1\},0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x]_{[0,1]}:=\max\{\min\{x,1\},0\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any non-singular <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑷</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., where 1 is not an entry of <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑷</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}</annotation></semantics></math>), we can verify that:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{F_{\bm{P}}(x)}{F_{0}(x)}=0~~\forall x\in(0,1-P_{(1)})~~\implies~~\lim_{x\to 0}\frac{F_{\bm{P}}(x)}{F_{0}(x)}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.827em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.660em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.660em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{F_{\bm{P}}(x)}{F_{0}(x)}=0~~\forall x\in(0,1-P_{(1)})~~\implies~~\lim_{x\to 0}\frac{F_{\bm{P}}(x)}{F_{0}(x)}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, both watermarks satisfy Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ Identifiability for continuous pivotal statistics. ‣ 3.2 Estimability ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlem4" title="Lemma 3.4 (Optimal weight function). ‣ Optimal weight function. ‣ 3.3 Estimation Methods ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a></h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlem4" title="Lemma 3.4 (Optimal weight function). ‣ Optimal weight function. ‣ 3.3 Estimation Methods ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We aim to maximize the following functional</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}(v)=\frac{\left(\mathbb{E}_{0}[v]-\mathbb{E}_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[v]\right)^{2}}{\text{Var}_{\bar{F}}(v)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msub><mtext>Var</mtext><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}(v)=\frac{\left(\mathbb{E}_{0}[v]-\mathbb{E}_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[v]\right)^{2}}{\text{Var}_{\bar{F}}(v)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the function to optimize and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)=\frac{{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}}{{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}}(x)-\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}{{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)=\frac{{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}}{{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}}(x)-\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}{{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">In the main text, we use the equivalent form of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)=\frac{1-g(x)}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}g(x)}~~\text{where}~~g(x)=\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}{{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>where</mtext><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)=\frac{1-g(x)}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}g(x)}~~\text{where}~~g(x)=\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}{{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The first step is to simplify the expression for <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}(v)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using the definition of <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)</annotation></semantics></math>, its numerator becomes:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{0}[v]-\mathbb{E}_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[v]=\int v(x)\left({\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)\right)=\int v(x)v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{0}[v]-\mathbb{E}_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[v]=\int v(x)\left({\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)\right)=\int v(x)v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we analyze the denominator. Assume, without loss of generality, that <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is centered under <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int v(x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int v(x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="A1.SS2.p2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is because adding a constant does not affect the value of <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}(v)</annotation></semantics></math>; that is, <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}(v)={\mathcal{L}}(v+C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}(v)={\mathcal{L}}(v+C)</annotation></semantics></math> for any constant <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Then:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{\bar{F}}(v)=\int v^{2}(x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)-\left(\int v(x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)\right)^{2}=\int v^{2}(x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{\bar{F}}(v)=\int v^{2}(x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)-\left(\int v(x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)\right)^{2}=\int v^{2}(x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the objective simplifies to:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}(v)=\frac{\left(\int v(x)v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)\right)^{2}}{\int v^{2}(x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}(v)=\frac{\left(\int v(x)v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)\right)^{2}}{\int v^{2}(x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, for two functions <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)</annotation></semantics></math> under the measure <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\int v(x)v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)\right)^{2}\leq\left(\int v^{2}(x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)\right)\left(\int v_{\mathrm{opt}}^{2}({\varepsilon},x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>opt</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\int v(x)v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)\right)^{2}\leq\left(\int v^{2}(x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)\right)\left(\int v_{\mathrm{opt}}^{2}({\varepsilon},x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Equality holds if and only if <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is proportional to <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. for some constant <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(x)=c\cdot v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(x)=c\cdot v_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, plugging this optimal weight function, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}(v_{\mathrm{opt}})=\frac{\left(\int v_{\mathrm{opt}}^{2}({\varepsilon},x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)\right)^{2}}{\int v_{\mathrm{opt}}^{2}({\varepsilon},x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)}=\int\frac{({\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(x))^{2}}{{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)}=\int\frac{(1-g(x))^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}g(x)}{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>opt</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>opt</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}(v_{\mathrm{opt}})=\frac{\left(\int v_{\mathrm{opt}}^{2}({\varepsilon},x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)\right)^{2}}{\int v_{\mathrm{opt}}^{2}({\varepsilon},x){\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)}=\int\frac{({\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(x))^{2}}{{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)}=\int\frac{(1-g(x))^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}g(x)}{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Proof of Inequality (<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Optimal weight function. ‣ 3.3 Estimation Methods ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Inequality (<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Optimal weight function. ‣ 3.3 Estimation Methods ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we prove the following inequality</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\EB_{{F}_{0}}[v]-\EB_{\widehat{F}}[v]}{\EB_{{F}_{0}}[v]-\EB_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[v]}\right)\leq\frac{\mathrm{Var}_{\bar{F}}(v)}{n(\EB_{{F}_{0}}[v]-\EB_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[v])^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\EB_{{F}_{0}}[v]-\EB_{\widehat{F}}[v]}{\EB_{{F}_{0}}[v]-\EB_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[v]}\right)\leq\frac{\mathrm{Var}_{\bar{F}}(v)}{n(\EB_{{F}_{0}}[v]-\EB_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[v])^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Optimal weight function. ‣ 3.3 Estimation Methods ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that under Model 2, <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is the empirical CDF of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> independent pivotal statistics <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{1},\ldots,Y_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> where each <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{t}\sim(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{t}\sim(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
It then follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\EB_{{F}_{0}}[v]-\EB_{\widehat{F}}[v]}{\EB_{{F}_{0}}[v]-\EB_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[v]}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\EB_{{F}_{0}}[v]-\EB_{\widehat{F}}[v]}{\EB_{{F}_{0}}[v]-\EB_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[v]}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathrm{Var}(\EB_{\widehat{F}}[v])}{(\EB_{{F}_{0}}[v]-\EB_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[v])^{2}}=\frac{\mathrm{Var}(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}v(Y_{t}))}{(\EB_{{F}_{0}}[v]-\EB_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[v])^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathrm{Var}(\EB_{\widehat{F}}[v])}{(\EB_{{F}_{0}}[v]-\EB_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[v])^{2}}=\frac{\mathrm{Var}(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}v(Y_{t}))}{(\EB_{{F}_{0}}[v]-\EB_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[v])^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{t=1}^{n}\mathrm{Var}_{(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}}(v)}{n^{2}(\EB_{{F}_{0}}[v]-\EB_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[v])^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{t=1}^{n}\mathrm{Var}_{(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}}(v)}{n^{2}(\EB_{{F}_{0}}[v]-\EB_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[v])^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Using the notation <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bar{F}=(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}\cdot\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{F}=(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}\cdot\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we then complete the proof by</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\mathrm{Var}_{(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\mathrm{Var}_{(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}}(v)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}[\EB_{(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}}[v^{2}]-(\EB_{(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}}[v])^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}[\EB_{(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}}[v^{2}]-(\EB_{(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}}[v])^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\EB_{(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}}[v^{2}]-\left(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\EB_{(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}}[v]\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\EB_{(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}}[v^{2}]-\left(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}\EB_{(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}}[v]\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\EB_{\bar{F}}[v^{2}]-(\EB_{\bar{F}}[v])^{2}=\mathrm{Var}_{\bar{F}}(v)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\EB_{\bar{F}}[v^{2}]-(\EB_{\bar{F}}[v])^{2}=\mathrm{Var}_{\bar{F}}(v).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Analysis for the Initial Estimator</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first present the proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.1 Accuracy for Initial Attempts ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> and then discuss the MAE associated with adaptively tuning the parameter <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.1 Accuracy for Initial Attempts ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{F}=(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{F}=(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have the following decomposition:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta)=1-\frac{\widehat{F}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}=\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)-\widehat{F}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}-{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}+{\varepsilon}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ini</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta)=1-\frac{\widehat{F}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}=\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)-\widehat{F}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}-{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}+{\varepsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">We denote by <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}({\varepsilon})=(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}(\delta)+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}({\varepsilon})=(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}(\delta)+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> for simplicity.
Due to the relation (<a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 3.3 Estimation Methods ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), we have <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{F}(\delta)=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}p_{t}({\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{F}(\delta)=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}p_{t}({\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>.
It then follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\EB\left|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta)-{\varepsilon}+{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ini</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\EB\left|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta)-{\varepsilon}+{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\leq}\sqrt{\EB\left|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta)-{\varepsilon}+{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}\right|^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ini</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\leq}\sqrt{\EB\left|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta)-{\varepsilon}+{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}\right|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{\EB\left|\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)-\widehat{F}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}\right|^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{\EB\left|\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)-\widehat{F}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}\right|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{F_{0}(\delta)n}\sqrt{\sum_{t=1}^{n}p_{t}({\varepsilon})(1-p_{t}({\varepsilon}))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{F_{0}(\delta)n}\sqrt{\sum_{t=1}^{n}p_{t}({\varepsilon})(1-p_{t}({\varepsilon}))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\leq}\frac{1}{F_{0}(\delta)\sqrt{n}}\cdot\sqrt{\left[\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}p_{t}({\varepsilon})\right]\left(1-\left[\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}p_{t}({\varepsilon})\right]\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\leq}\frac{1}{F_{0}(\delta)\sqrt{n}}\cdot\sqrt{\left[\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}p_{t}({\varepsilon})\right]\left(1-\left[\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}p_{t}({\varepsilon})\right]\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(c)}{=}\frac{\sigma_{n}}{\sqrt{n}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(c)}{=}\frac{\sigma_{n}}{\sqrt{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)</annotation></semantics></math> follow from Jensen’s inequality, and <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c)</annotation></semantics></math> utilizes the definition of <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> that is <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{n}^{2}=\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)(1-\bar{F}(\delta))}{[F_{0}(\delta)]^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{n}^{2}=\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)(1-\bar{F}(\delta))}{[F_{0}(\delta)]^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math>
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.1 Accuracy for Initial Attempts ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> analyzes the mean absolute error (MAE) of <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ini</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> and shows it is of the order <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sigma_{n}}{\sqrt{n}}+\text{bias}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mtext>bias</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sigma_{n}}{\sqrt{n}}+\text{bias}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the bias term is given by <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4.4. ‣ 4.3 Minimax Lower Bounds ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a> establishes that the minimax optimal MAE within the class of all measurable functions of the indicator variables <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bf 1}\{Y_{1}\leq\delta\},\ldots,{\bf 1}\{Y_{n}\leq\delta\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bf 1}\{Y_{1}\leq\delta\},\ldots,{\bf 1}\{Y_{n}\leq\delta\}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sigma_{n}^{\star}}{\sqrt{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sigma_{n}^{\star}}{\sqrt{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.1 Accuracy for Initial Attempts ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, the variance term <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ini</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> is given by <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)(1-\bar{F}(\delta))}{[F_{0}(\delta)]^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)(1-\bar{F}(\delta))}{[F_{0}(\delta)]^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. As shown in Proposition <a href="#A1.Thmprop1" title="Proposition A.1. ‣ A.4 Analysis for the Initial Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, this variance is smaller (up to constant factors) than the optimal variance <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{n}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{n}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. However, the bias term <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}</annotation></semantics></math> generally increases the MAE of <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ini</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>, making its overall MAE larger than <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sigma_{n}^{\star}}{\sqrt{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sigma_{n}^{\star}}{\sqrt{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is further detailed in Corollary <a href="#Thmcor3" title="Corollary 3. ‣ A.4 Analysis for the Initial Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmprop1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmprop1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmprop1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmprop1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmprop1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmprop1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ Identifiability for continuous pivotal statistics. ‣ 3.2 Estimability ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, we have <math id="A1.Thmprop1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\cdot\sigma_{n}\leq\sigma_{n}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\cdot\sigma_{n}\leq\sigma_{n}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A1.Thmprop1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, where</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{n}^{2}=\frac{\bar{F}({\varepsilon})(1-\bar{F}({\varepsilon}))}{[F_{0}(\delta)]^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{n}^{2}=\frac{\bar{F}({\varepsilon})(1-\bar{F}({\varepsilon}))}{[F_{0}(\delta)]^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#A1.Thmprop1" title="Proposition A.1. ‣ A.4 Analysis for the Initial Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We observe that under Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 3.1. ‣ Identifiability for continuous pivotal statistics. ‣ 3.2 Estimability ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\delta\to 0}\frac{F_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\delta\to 0}\frac{F_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)}=0</annotation></semantics></math> ensuring that there exists a positive constant <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="A1.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|F_{0}(\delta)-F_{\bm{P}}(\delta)|\leq cF_{0}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|F_{0}(\delta)-F_{\bm{P}}(\delta)|\leq cF_{0}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑷</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, due to the continuity of <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\bm{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\bm{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑷</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.
It implies that we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{n}^{2}=\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)(1-\bar{F}(\delta))}{[F_{0}(\delta)]^{2}}\leq c^{2}\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)(1-\bar{F}(\delta))}{[F_{0}(\delta)-\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)]^{2}}=c^{2}\cdot[\sigma_{n}^{\star}]^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{n}^{2}=\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)(1-\bar{F}(\delta))}{[F_{0}(\delta)]^{2}}\leq c^{2}\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)(1-\bar{F}(\delta))}{[F_{0}(\delta)-\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)]^{2}}=c^{2}\cdot[\sigma_{n}^{\star}]^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmcor3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcor3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 3</span></span><span id="Thmcor3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcor3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcor3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcor3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the same setting as Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.1 Accuracy for Initial Attempts ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, assume that <math id="Thmcor3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)\sim x^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)\sim x^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmcor3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}(x)\sim x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}(x)\sim x</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="Thmcor3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmcor3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, if <math id="Thmcor3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}=\Theta(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}=\Theta(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB\left|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta_{n})-{\varepsilon}\right|\leq\frac{\sigma_{n}}{\sqrt{n}}+{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta_{n})}{F_{0}(\delta_{n})}\sim\frac{1}{\sqrt{n\delta_{n}}}+{\varepsilon}\delta_{n}^{p-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ini</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB\left|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta_{n})-{\varepsilon}\right|\leq\frac{\sigma_{n}}{\sqrt{n}}+{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta_{n})}{F_{0}(\delta_{n})}\sim\frac{1}{\sqrt{n\delta_{n}}}+{\varepsilon}\delta_{n}^{p-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmcor3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcor3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">By selecting the optimal value <math id="Thmcor3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{n}=[2(p-1){\varepsilon}\sqrt{n}]^{-\frac{1}{p-0.5}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{n}=[2(p-1){\varepsilon}\sqrt{n}]^{-\frac{1}{p-0.5}}</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB\left|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta_{n})-{\varepsilon}\right|\precsim\frac{{\varepsilon}^{\frac{1}{p-0.5}}}{n^{\frac{1}{2}\left(1-\frac{1}{p-0.5}\right)}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ini</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≾</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ε</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB\left|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta_{n})-{\varepsilon}\right|\precsim\frac{{\varepsilon}^{\frac{1}{p-0.5}}}{n^{\frac{1}{2}\left(1-\frac{1}{p-0.5}\right)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This result highlights that the bias term <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta_{n})}{F_{0}(\delta_{n})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta_{n})}{F_{0}(\delta_{n})}</annotation></semantics></math> limits the performance of <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ini</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>. Even with adaptive tuning of <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, its dependence on <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly slower than <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, illustrating why <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ini</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{ini}}}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> cannot achieve minimax optimality.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Analysis for the Refined Estimator</h4>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Full version of the first part in Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.2 Accuracy for Refinements ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> be fixed. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB\left|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{rfn}}}(\delta)-{\varepsilon}+{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}\right|\leq\frac{\widehat{\sigma}_{n}}{\sqrt{n}},~~\text{where}~~\widehat{\sigma}_{n}^{2}=\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)(1-\bar{F}(\delta))}{[F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)]^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>rfn</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">where</mtext><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB\left|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{rfn}}}(\delta)-{\varepsilon}+{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}\right|\leq\frac{\widehat{\sigma}_{n}}{\sqrt{n}},~~\text{where}~~\widehat{\sigma}_{n}^{2}=\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)(1-\bar{F}(\delta))}{[F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)]^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmcor4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcor4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 4</span></span><span id="Thmcor4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Simplified MAE)<span id="Thmcor4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcor4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcor4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcor4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When <math id="Thmcor4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{x}\frac{|\widehat{g}(x)-g(x)|}{\min\{1,\widehat{g}(x)\}}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{x}\frac{|\widehat{g}(x)-g(x)|}{\min\{1,\widehat{g}(x)\}}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="Thmcor4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\sigma}_{n}\to\sigma_{n}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\sigma}_{n}\to\sigma_{n}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, implying <math id="Thmcor4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{n}^{\star}=\widehat{\sigma}_{n}+o_{g}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{n}^{\star}=\widehat{\sigma}_{n}+o_{g}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Under this condition, the bias term <math id="Thmcor4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}</annotation></semantics></math> also becomes <math id="Thmcor4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{g}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{g}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{rfn}}}(\delta)-{\varepsilon}|\leq\frac{\sigma_{n}^{\star}+o_{g}(1)}{\sqrt{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>rfn</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{rfn}}}(\delta)-{\varepsilon}|\leq\frac{\sigma_{n}^{\star}+o_{g}(1)}{\sqrt{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem A.1 (Full version of the first part in Theorem ). ‣ A.5 Analysis for the Refined Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{F}=(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{F}=(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}+{\varepsilon}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have the following decomposition:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{rfn}}}(\delta)=\frac{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}=\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)-\widehat{F}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}-{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}+{\varepsilon}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>rfn</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{rfn}}}(\delta)=\frac{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}=\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)-\widehat{F}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}-{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}+{\varepsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">We denote by <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}({\varepsilon})=(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}(\delta)+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}({\varepsilon})=(1-{\varepsilon})F_{0}(\delta)+{\varepsilon}F_{\bm{P}_{t}}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> for simplicity.
Due to the relation (<a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ 3.3 Estimation Methods ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), we have <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{F}(\delta)=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}p_{t}({\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{F}(\delta)=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}p_{t}({\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>.
It then follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\EB\left|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{rfn}}}(\delta)-{\varepsilon}+{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>rfn</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\EB\left|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{rfn}}}(\delta)-{\varepsilon}+{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\leq}\sqrt{\EB\left|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{rfn}}}(\delta)-{\varepsilon}+{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}\right|^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>rfn</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{\leq}\sqrt{\EB\left|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{rfn}}}(\delta)-{\varepsilon}+{\varepsilon}\frac{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}\right|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{\EB\left|\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)-\widehat{F}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}\right|^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{\EB\left|\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)-\widehat{F}(\delta)}{F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)}\right|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\sum_{t=1}^{n}p_{t}({\varepsilon})(1-p_{t}({\varepsilon}))}}{n[F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{\sum_{t=1}^{n}p_{t}({\varepsilon})(1-p_{t}({\varepsilon}))}}{n[F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\leq}\frac{\sqrt{\left[\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}p_{t}({\varepsilon})\right]\left(1-\left[\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}p_{t}({\varepsilon})\right]\right)}}{\sqrt{n}[F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\leq}\frac{\sqrt{\left[\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}p_{t}({\varepsilon})\right]\left(1-\left[\frac{1}{n}\sum_{t=1}^{n}p_{t}({\varepsilon})\right]\right)}}{\sqrt{n}[F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(c)}{=}\frac{\widehat{\sigma}_{n}}{\sqrt{n}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(c)}{=}\frac{\widehat{\sigma}_{n}}{\sqrt{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b)</annotation></semantics></math> follow from Jensen’s inequality, and <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c)</annotation></semantics></math> utilizes the definition of <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\sigma}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\sigma}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> that is <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\sigma}_{n}^{2}=\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)(1-\bar{F}(\delta))}{[F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)]^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\sigma}_{n}^{2}=\frac{\bar{F}(\delta)(1-\bar{F}(\delta))}{[F_{0}(\delta)-\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(\delta)]^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math>
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Analysis for the Optimal Estimator</h4>

<section id="A1.SS6.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.6.1 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlem5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ Optimal weight function. ‣ 3.3 Estimation Methods ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a></h5>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that we define an operator <math id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{{\mathcal{T}}}:[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]\to[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{{\mathcal{T}}}:[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]\to[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]</annotation></semantics></math> in defining the optimal estimator <math id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{opt}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>opt</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{opt}}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})={\mathcal{P}}\circ\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})~~\text{with}~~\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon}):=\frac{\int\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)\left[{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}(x)\right]}{\int\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)\left[{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)\right]}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>with</mtext><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})={\mathcal{P}}\circ\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})~~\text{with}~~\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon}):=\frac{\int\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)\left[{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}(x)\right]}{\int\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)\left[{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)\right]},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{P}}(x):=\max\{\min\{x,1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}\},{\varepsilon}_{\min}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{P}}(x):=\max\{\min\{x,1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}\},{\varepsilon}_{\min}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the projection operator, and <math id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}_{\min}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}_{\min}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a small constant to avoid numerical issues.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To establish Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlem5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ Optimal weight function. ‣ 3.3 Estimation Methods ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>, which asserts that <math id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{{\mathcal{T}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{{\mathcal{T}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a contraction mapping with high probability, we first derive a supporting result, stated as Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ A.6.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>. The proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ A.6.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> is deferred to Appendix <a href="#A1.SS6.SSS3" title="A.6.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define the total variation distance between <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> as
<math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{TV}}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}):=\frac{1}{2}\int|1-\widehat{g}(x)|{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{TV}}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}):=\frac{1}{2}\int|1-\widehat{g}(x)|{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{g}:=\max\{1,\sup\limits_{x\in[0,1]}|\widehat{g}(x)|\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{g}:=\max\{1,\sup\limits_{x\in[0,1]}|\widehat{g}(x)|\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume that <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{TV}}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{TV}}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{g}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{g}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{g}=\sup\limits_{x\in[0,1]}\frac{|\widehat{g}(x)-g(x)|}{\min\{1,\widehat{g}(x)\}}~~\text{and}~~C_{0}=\frac{C_{g}^{2}}{2D_{\mathrm{TV}}^{3}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{g}=\sup\limits_{x\in[0,1]}\frac{|\widehat{g}(x)-g(x)|}{\min\{1,\widehat{g}(x)\}}~~\text{and}~~C_{0}=\frac{C_{g}^{2}}{2D_{\mathrm{TV}}^{3}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, for some positive constant <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the following results hold:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="4"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E15.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}-\EB\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|\geq\frac{C_{0}}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{C\log n}{n}}\right)\leq\frac{8K}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{3}}\cdot\frac{1}{n^{C-1}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}-\EB\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|\geq\frac{C_{0}}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{C\log n}{n}}\right)\leq\frac{8K}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{3}}\cdot\frac{1}{n^{C-1}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E15.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\EB\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|\leq\Delta_{g}\left[1+C_{0}\min\left\{\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}},\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{3}+\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}\right\}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\EB\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|\leq\Delta_{g}\left[1+C_{0}\min\left\{\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}},\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{3}+\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}\right\}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15b)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If we further have <math id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{\bar{F}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{\bar{F}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, then (<a href="#A1.E15.1" title="Equation 15a ‣ Equation 15 ‣ Lemma A.1. ‣ A.6.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15a</span></a>) can be refined to</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}-\EB\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|\geq C_{0}^{\prime}\left[\frac{C\log n}{n{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{2}}+\sqrt{\frac{CM\log n}{n{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{2}}}\right]\right)\leq\frac{8K}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{3}}\cdot\frac{1}{n^{C-1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}-\EB\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|\geq C_{0}^{\prime}\left[\frac{C\log n}{n{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{2}}+\sqrt{\frac{CM\log n}{n{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{2}}}\right]\right)\leq\frac{8K}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{3}}\cdot\frac{1}{n^{C-1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15c)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmlem1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}^{\prime}:=\frac{C_{g}^{2}\left[\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{3}+\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}\right]}{D_{\mathrm{TV}}^{4}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}})}\quad\text{and}\quad M:=8\EB_{\bar{F}}\left[\widehat{g}-1/\widehat{g}\right]^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}^{\prime}:=\frac{C_{g}^{2}\left[\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{3}+\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}\right]}{D_{\mathrm{TV}}^{4}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}})}\quad\text{and}\quad M:=8\EB_{\bar{F}}\left[\widehat{g}-1/\widehat{g}\right]^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlem5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ Optimal weight function. ‣ 3.3 Estimation Methods ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> is a direct corollary of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ A.6.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>. Another useful consequence of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ A.6.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> is that it guarantees, with high probability, the quantity <math id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup\limits_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup\limits_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by a small value <math id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> (see Corollary <a href="#Thmcor5" title="Corollary 5 (Full version of Lemma ). ‣ A.6.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmcor5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcor5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 5</span></span><span id="Thmcor5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Full version of Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmlem5" title="Lemma 3.5. ‣ Optimal weight function. ‣ 3.3 Estimation Methods ‣ 3 Proportion Estimation Methods ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>)<span id="Thmcor5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcor5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcor5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcor5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the same assumptions and notations in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ A.6.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, for any <math id="Thmcor5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="Thmcor5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{8K}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{3}}\cdot\frac{1}{n^{C-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{8K}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{3}}\cdot\frac{1}{n^{C-1}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|\leq A," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|\leq A,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmcor5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcor5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the bound <math id="Thmcor5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> takes the following form depending on whether a moment condition holds:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{\bar{F}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{\bar{F}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (so that </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> also holds), the bound </span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is given by</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A=\Delta_{g}\left[1+C_{0}\left(\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{3}+\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}\right)\right]+C_{0}^{\prime}\left[\frac{C\log n}{n{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{2}}+\sqrt{\frac{CM\log n}{n{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{2}}}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A=\Delta_{g}\left[1+C_{0}\left(\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{3}+\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}\right)\right]+C_{0}^{\prime}\left[\frac{C\log n}{n{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{2}}+\sqrt{\frac{CM\log n}{n{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{2}}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If the moment condition </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{\bar{F}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{\bar{F}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> fails, the bound </span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> becomes</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A=\Delta_{g}\left[1+\frac{C_{0}}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}}\right]+\frac{C_{0}}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{C\log n}{n}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A=\Delta_{g}\left[1+\frac{C_{0}}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}}\right]+\frac{C_{0}}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{C\log n}{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Corollary <a href="#Thmcor5" title="Corollary 5 (Full version of Lemma ). ‣ A.6.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that the projection operator enforces the derivative to be zero only when its output lies outside the domain <math id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|\leq\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em">|</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|\leq\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#A1.E15.2" title="Equation 15b ‣ Equation 15 ‣ Lemma A.1. ‣ A.6.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15b</span></a>) in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ A.6.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, it follows that or any <math id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℙ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathbb{P}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|\geq x+\Delta_{g}\left[1+\frac{C_{0}}{4}\min\left\{\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{2}},\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{3}+\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}\right\}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|\geq x+\Delta_{g}\left[1+\frac{C_{0}}{4}\min\left\{\frac{1}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{2}},\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{3}+\EB_{F_{0}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}\right\}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|-\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\EB\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|\geq x\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|-\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\EB\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|\geq x\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}-\EB\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|\geq x\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq{\mathbb{P}}\left(\sup_{{\varepsilon}\in[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]}\left|\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}-\EB\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}\right|\geq x\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">By setting <math id="A1.SS6.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\frac{C_{0}}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{C\log n}{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\frac{C_{0}}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{C\log n}{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> and applying (<a href="#A1.E15.1" title="Equation 15a ‣ Equation 15 ‣ Lemma A.1. ‣ A.6.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15a</span></a>), we complete the proof of the second bullet point. The proof of the first bullet point is similar and is therefore omitted.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.6.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.2 Accuracy for Refinements ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a></h5>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The first part of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.2 Accuracy for Refinements ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> concerns the accuracy of the refined estimator <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{rfn}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>rfn</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{rfn}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with its analysis provided in Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem A.1 (Full version of the first part in Theorem ). ‣ A.5 Analysis for the Refined Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>. The second part addresses the accuracy of the optimal estimator <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{opt}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>opt</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{opt}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is analyzed in Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem A.2 (Full version of the second part of Theorem ; proof in Appendix ). ‣ A.6.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>. The inequality that <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{n}^{\star}\geq\tau_{n}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{n}^{\star}\geq\tau_{n}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is established at the end of Appendix <a href="#A1.SS8" title="A.8 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Full version of the second part of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 4.2. ‣ 4.2 Accuracy for Refinements ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>; proof in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS6.SSS4" title="A.6.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6.4</span></a>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;D_{\mathrm{TV}}(\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}},F_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;D_{\mathrm{TV}}(\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}},F_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup\limits_{x}|\widehat{g}(x)|&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>x</mi></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup\limits_{x}|\widehat{g}(x)|&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{g}:=\max\{1,\sup_{x\in[0,1]}\widehat{g}(x)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{g}:=\max\{1,\sup_{x\in[0,1]}\widehat{g}(x)\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex10a" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{g}=\sup\limits_{x\in[0,1]}\frac{|\widehat{g}(x)-g(x)|}{\min\{1,\widehat{g}(x)\}}~~\text{and}~~C_{0}=\frac{C_{g}^{2}}{D_{\mathrm{TV}}^{3}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{g}=\sup\limits_{x\in[0,1]}\frac{|\widehat{g}(x)-g(x)|}{\min\{1,\widehat{g}(x)\}}~~\text{and}~~C_{0}=\frac{C_{g}^{2}}{D_{\mathrm{TV}}^{3}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a fixed true proportion <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\EB|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{opt}}}-{\varepsilon}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\EB|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{opt}}}-{\varepsilon}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11a.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(1-A\right)^{-1}\left({\mathcal{V}}+{\mathcal{B}}+{\varepsilon}_{\min}{\bf 1}\{{\varepsilon}\notin[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]\}\right)+\frac{8K}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{3}}\cdot\frac{1}{n^{C-1}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(1-A\right)^{-1}\left({\mathcal{V}}+{\mathcal{B}}+{\varepsilon}_{\min}{\bf 1}\{{\varepsilon}\notin[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]\}\right)+\frac{8K}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}^{3}}\cdot\frac{1}{n^{C-1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is any given positive constant, the expression of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is given in Corollary <a href="#Thmcor5" title="Corollary 5 (Full version of Lemma ). ‣ A.6.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> (not restated here for brevity),
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K,C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K,C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> are problem-dependent constants defined in Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ A.6.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> are the variance and bias terms, respectively, defined as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex12a" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}=\frac{\sqrt{\frac{1}{n}\int\left[\frac{1-\widehat{g}(x)}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}(x)}\right]^{2}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)}}{\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}(x)]^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}(x)}{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)},~~\text{and}~~{\mathcal{B}}={\varepsilon}\left|\frac{\int\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)\left[{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)\right]}{\int\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)\left[{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)\right]}\right|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}=\frac{\sqrt{\frac{1}{n}\int\left[\frac{1-\widehat{g}(x)}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}(x)}\right]^{2}{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}(x)}}{\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}(x)]^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}(x)}{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)},~~\text{and}~~{\mathcal{B}}={\varepsilon}\left|\frac{\int\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)\left[{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)\right]}{\int\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)\left[{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)\right]}\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmcor6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcor6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 6</span></span><span id="Thmcor6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Simplified MAE)<span id="Thmcor6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcor6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcor6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcor6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="Thmcor6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;D_{\mathrm{TV}}(\bar{F}_{\bm{P}},F_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;D_{\mathrm{TV}}(\bar{F}_{\bm{P}},F_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmcor6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup\limits_{x}|{g}(x)|&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>x</mi></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup\limits_{x}|{g}(x)|&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmcor6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{F_{0}}[g]^{-2}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{F_{0}}[g]^{-2}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Thmcor6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{g}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{g}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> denote a term that converges to zero as <math id="Thmcor6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{g}:=\sup_{x}\frac{|\widehat{g}(x)-g(x)|}{\min\{1,\widehat{g}(x)\}}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{g}:=\sup_{x}\frac{|\widehat{g}(x)-g(x)|}{\min\{1,\widehat{g}(x)\}}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmcor6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o(1)</annotation></semantics></math> a term that converges to zero as <math id="Thmcor6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
If either setting <math id="Thmcor6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> as a small constant or choosing <math id="Thmcor6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}_{\min}=\frac{\log n}{\sqrt{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}_{\min}=\frac{\log n}{\sqrt{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we then have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex13a" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=o_{g}(1)+o(1),\quad{\mathcal{B}}=o_{g}(1),\quad{\mathcal{V}}=\frac{\tau_{n}^{\star}+o_{g}(1)}{\sqrt{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=o_{g}(1)+o(1),\quad{\mathcal{B}}=o_{g}(1),\quad{\mathcal{V}}=\frac{\tau_{n}^{\star}+o_{g}(1)}{\sqrt{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmcor6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcor6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">As a result, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex14a" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14a.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\EB|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{opt}}}-{\varepsilon}|\precsim\frac{\tau_{n}^{\star}+o(1)}{\sqrt{n}}+o_{g}(1)+{\varepsilon}_{\min}{\bf 1}\{{\varepsilon}\notin[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≾</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB|{\widehat{{\varepsilon}}_{\mathrm{opt}}}-{\varepsilon}|\precsim\frac{\tau_{n}^{\star}+o(1)}{\sqrt{n}}+o_{g}(1)+{\varepsilon}_{\min}{\bf 1}\{{\varepsilon}\notin[{\varepsilon}_{\min},1-{\varepsilon}_{\min}]\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmcor6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcor6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The last inequality also holds without the condition <math id="Thmcor6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{F_{0}}[g]^{-2}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{F_{0}}[g]^{-2}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> given that we set <math id="Thmcor6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}_{\min}=\frac{\log n}{n^{1/4}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}_{\min}=\frac{\log n}{n^{1/4}}</annotation></semantics></math> and ensure that <math id="Thmcor6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{1/4}\cdot\Delta_{g}=o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{1/4}\cdot\Delta_{g}=o(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Corollary <a href="#Thmcor6" title="Corollary 6 (Simplified MAE). ‣ A.6.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">It suffices to simplify the variance term <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the bias term <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in Theorem <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem A.2 (Full version of the second part of Theorem ; proof in Appendix ). ‣ A.6.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>.
Let <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{g}=\sup\limits_{x}\frac{|\widehat{g}(x)-g(x)|}{\min\{1,\widehat{g}(x)\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>x</mi></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{g}=\sup\limits_{x}\frac{|\widehat{g}(x)-g(x)|}{\min\{1,\widehat{g}(x)\}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the uniform estiamtion error between <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a continuous functional of the density ratio <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, as <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{g}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{g}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15a" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{V}}\to\left[\frac{1}{n}\int\frac{[1-g(x)]^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}g(x)}{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)\right]^{-\frac{1}{2}}=\frac{\tau_{n}^{\star}}{\sqrt{n}}~~\implies~~{\mathcal{V}}=\frac{\tau_{n}^{\star}+o_{g}(1)}{\sqrt{n}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.938em" rspace="0.938em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{V}}\to\left[\frac{1}{n}\int\frac{[1-g(x)]^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}g(x)}{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)\right]^{-\frac{1}{2}}=\frac{\tau_{n}^{\star}}{\sqrt{n}}~~\implies~~{\mathcal{V}}=\frac{\tau_{n}^{\star}+o_{g}(1)}{\sqrt{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{g}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{g}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> denote a quantity that converges to zero when <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> converges to zero.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We then analyze the bias term <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The numerator of the term <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex16a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\int\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)\left[{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)\right]\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\int\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)\left[{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)\right]\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left|\int\frac{(1-\widehat{g}(x))(\widehat{g}(x)-g(x))}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}(x)}{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left|\int\frac{(1-\widehat{g}(x))(\widehat{g}(x)-g(x))}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}(x)}{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\Delta_{g}\cdot\int|1-\widehat{g}(x)|{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)=2\Delta_{g}\cdot D_{\mathrm{TV}}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\Delta_{g}\cdot\int|1-\widehat{g}(x)|{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)=2\Delta_{g}\cdot D_{\mathrm{TV}}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the denominator, by (<a href="#A1.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ Item 
                        
                          
                            
                            
                              (
                              c
                              ) ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ A.6.3 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\int\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)\left[{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)\right]\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\int\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)\left[{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)\right]\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}(x)]^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}(x)}{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}(x)]^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}(x)}{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex19a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{D_{\chi^{2}}(\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}},F_{0})}{C_{g}}\geq\frac{4}{C_{g}}D_{\mathrm{TV}}^{2}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{D_{\chi^{2}}(\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}},F_{0})}{C_{g}}\geq\frac{4}{C_{g}}D_{\mathrm{TV}}^{2}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Here, <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{g}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{g}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> represents the upper bound of <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\widehat{g}(x)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\widehat{g}(x)|</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup\limits_{x}|g(x)|&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>x</mi></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup\limits_{x}|g(x)|&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{g}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{g}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{g}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{g}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. This ensures that the bounds involving <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> remain finite under the given assumptions.
Combining these bounds, the bias term is bounded by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex20a" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{B}}\leq\frac{C_{g}\Delta_{g}}{2D_{\mathrm{TV}}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}})}=o_{g}(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{B}}\leq\frac{C_{g}\Delta_{g}}{2D_{\mathrm{TV}}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}})}=o_{g}(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">The last equation uses the fact that as <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{g}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{g}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the total variation distance <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{TV}}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}})\to D_{\mathrm{TV}}(F_{0},\bar{F}_{\bm{P}})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{TV}}(F_{0},\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}})\to D_{\mathrm{TV}}(F_{0},\bar{F}_{\bm{P}})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now suppose the moment condition <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{F_{0}}[g]^{-2}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{F_{0}}[g]^{-2}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> holds. This implies that <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[g]^{-2}=\EB_{F_{0}}[g]^{-1}\leq\sqrt{\EB_{F_{0}}[g]^{-2}}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[g]^{-2}=\EB_{F_{0}}[g]^{-1}\leq\sqrt{\EB_{F_{0}}[g]^{-2}}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{\bar{F}}[g]^{-2}\leq\max\{\EB_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[g]^{-2},\EB_{F_{0}}[g]^{-2}\}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>𝐏</mi></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{\bar{F}}[g]^{-2}\leq\max\{\EB_{\bar{F}_{\bm{P}}}[g]^{-2},\EB_{F_{0}}[g]^{-2}\}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
When <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{g}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{g}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)\leq(1+\Delta_{g})\widehat{g}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)\leq(1+\Delta_{g})\widehat{g}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{\bar{F}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}\leq(1+\Delta_{g})^{2}\EB_{\bar{F}}[g]^{-2}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{\bar{F}}[\widehat{g}]^{-2}\leq(1+\Delta_{g})^{2}\EB_{\bar{F}}[g]^{-2}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. This confirms that the moment condition in Corollary <a href="#Thmcor5" title="Corollary 5 (Full version of Lemma ). ‣ A.6.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> holds.
If <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> is set as a small constant, then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex21a" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A={\mathcal{O}}\left(\Delta_{g}+\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{n}}\right)=o_{g}(1)+o(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A={\mathcal{O}}\left(\Delta_{g}+\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{n}}\right)=o_{g}(1)+o(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">If we set <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}_{\min}=\log n/\sqrt{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}_{\min}=\log n/\sqrt{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex22a" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A={\mathcal{O}}\left(\Delta_{g}+\frac{1}{\log n}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{\log n}}\right)=o_{g}(1)+o(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A={\mathcal{O}}\left(\Delta_{g}+\frac{1}{\log n}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{\log n}}\right)=o_{g}(1)+o(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Without the moment condition <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{F_{0}}[g]^{-2}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{F_{0}}[g]^{-2}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</h6>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, if the moment condition <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\EB_{F_{0}}[g]^{-2}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\EB_{F_{0}}[g]^{-2}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> does not hold, then we only have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex23a" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A={\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\Delta_{g}}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{\log^{3}n}}\right)={\mathcal{O}}\left(n^{1/4}\cdot\Delta_{g}\right)+o(1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>log</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A={\mathcal{O}}\left(\frac{\Delta_{g}}{{\varepsilon}_{\min}}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{\log^{3}n}}\right)={\mathcal{O}}\left(n^{1/4}\cdot\Delta_{g}\right)+o(1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS2.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">when we set <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}_{\min}=\frac{\log n}{n^{1/4}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}_{\min}=\frac{\log n}{n^{1/4}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
To ensure that the above <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=o(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we must impose the stronger requirement <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{1/4}\cdot\Delta_{g}=o(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{1/4}\cdot\Delta_{g}=o(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, which means the estimation error in <math id="A1.SS6.SSS2.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}</annotation></semantics></math> must be significantly smaller than in the previous two cases.
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.6.3 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ A.6.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a></h5>

<div id="A1.SS6.SSS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmlem1" title="Lemma A.1. ‣ A.6.1 Proof of Lemma ‣ A.6 Analysis for the Optimal Estimator ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Analysis ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">In the following, all integrations are taken with respect to <math id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. For simplicity, we omit explicit notation for the dependence on <math id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the definition of <math id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)</annotation></semantics></math>, and noting that <math id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}(x)=\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)}{{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}(x)=\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)}{{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}(x)}</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that for any <math id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex24a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})=\frac{\int\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)\left[{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}(x)\right]}{\int\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)\left[{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)\right]}=\frac{\int\frac{1-\widehat{g}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}}\left[{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}\right]}{\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}}{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>opt</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑷</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})=\frac{\int\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)\left[{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}(x)\right]}{\int\widehat{v}_{\mathrm{opt}}({\varepsilon},x)\left[{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}(x)-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}_{\bm{P}}(x)\right]}=\frac{\int\frac{1-\widehat{g}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}}\left[{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}\right]}{\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}}{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Direct calculation yields that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex25a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{2}}{[(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}]^{2}}\left[{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}\right]}{\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}}{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}}-\frac{\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{3}}{[(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}]^{2}}{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}}{\left[\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}}{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}\right]^{2}}\cdot\int\frac{1-\widehat{g}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}}\left[{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{2}}{[(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}]^{2}}\left[{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}\right]}{\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}}{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}}-\frac{\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{3}}{[(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}]^{2}}{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}}{\left[\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}}{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}\right]^{2}}\cdot\int\frac{1-\widehat{g}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}}\left[{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}-{\mathrm{d}}\widehat{F}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the expectation (with randomness only from <math id="A1.SS6.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{F}</annotation></semantics></math>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex26a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\EB\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\EB\frac{{\mathrm{d}}\widetilde{{\mathcal{T}}}({\varepsilon})}{{\mathrm{d}}{\varepsilon}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{2}}{[(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}]^{2}}\left[{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}-{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}\right]}{\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}}{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}}-\frac{\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{3}}{[(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}]^{2}}{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}}{\left[\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}}{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}\right]^{2}}\cdot\int\frac{1-\widehat{g}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}}\left[{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}-{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{2}}{[(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}]^{2}}\left[{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}-{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}\right]}{\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}}{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}}-\frac{\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{3}}{[(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}]^{2}}{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}}{\left[\int\frac{[1-\widehat{g}]^{2}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}}{\mathrm{d}}{F}_{0}\right]^{2}}\cdot\int\frac{1-\widehat{g}}{(1-{\varepsilon})+{\varepsilon}\widehat{g}}\left[{\mathrm{d}}F_{0}-{\mathrm{d}}\bar{F}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
