</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="A2.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">CDF plots of mixture distributions for the inverse transform watermark.
Here, <math id="A2.F4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> represents the dominance parameter used in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Failure on green-red list watermarks. ‣ B.1 Further Details ‣ Appendix B Simulation Study: Details and Results ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> for generating NTP distributions, and <math id="A2.F4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the true proportion.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Additional Results on Estimation Accuracy</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#A2.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ B.3 Additional Results on Estimation Accuracy ‣ Appendix B Simulation Study: Details and Results ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and <a href="#A2.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ B.3 Additional Results on Estimation Accuracy ‣ Appendix B Simulation Study: Details and Results ‣ Appendices ‣ Optimal Estimation of Watermark Proportions in Hybrid AI-Human Texts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> show the complete results of the estimation performance of various estimators on the Gumbel-max and inverse transform watermarks, respectively. In most cases, <span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">OPT</span> achieves the lowest MAE.</p>
</div>
